# chat: `hi` is answered by the code model (the `--mock` generator's one deterministic line) — a [you] bubble, a
# [jevcode] reply, no card, no run; Jev reads the message in the background and adds nothing here. The badge stays the
# default (llm+jev) and the wall time Enter → [jevcode] is read from the timing file (§8.2 chat-hi)
expect \x1b\[\?25l
expect Say hi
expect sess \$
sleep 0.2
send hi
sleep 0.2
send \r
mark hi-sent
expect \[you\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* (?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)*hi
expect \[jevcode\](?:\x1b\[[0-9;]*m)* Hi
mark hi-reply
expect llm\+jev · verified
send /exit
sleep 0.2
send \r
eof
